# Local build configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `secrets.properties` in the root of the repository, then
# uncomment and fill in the values you need:
#
#     cp secrets.properties-example secrets.properties
#
# `secrets.properties` is ignored by Git, so your credentials stay out of version
# control. Every value set here overrides the matching entry in
# `defaults.properties`, as well as any secrets applied by
# `bundle exec fastlane run configure_apply`. Entries left commented out keep
# their existing value, so you only need the ones you want to change.
#
# `wp.`-prefixed properties become `BuildConfig` fields in both apps, with the
# prefix dropped and the remaining separators replaced by underscores, e.g.
# `wp.oauth.app_id` is available as `BuildConfig.OAUTH_APP_ID`. A `jp.`-prefixed
# property of the same name takes precedence in the Jetpack app.
#
# WordPress.com credentials from https://developer.wordpress.com/apps/. See
# `docs/wpcom-authentication.md` for the full setup, which includes registering
# the redirect URLs the apps rely on.

#wp.oauth.app_id = your_client_id
#wp.oauth.app_secret = your_client_secret
